#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following helper functions are used by the large-scale hardware example later in the tutorial:\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ang mga sumusunod na helper function sa malakihang hardware example mamaya sa tutorial:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`bad_cz`, `bad_readout`, `bad_coherence` — Query the backend calibration data to identify gates, qubits, and edges that exceed error or coherence thresholds, so they can be excluded from the circuit layout.\n"
msgstr "`bad_cz`, `bad_readout`, `bad_coherence` — Nagqu-query ng backend calibration data para tukuyin ang mga gate, qubit, at edge na lumalampas sa mga error o coherence threshold, para maibukod ang mga ito sa circuit layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`parallel_ghz` — Builds a GHZ circuit of a given size using a breadth-first search over the coupling map, spreading CNOT layers in parallel to minimize circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "`parallel_ghz` — Bumubuo ng GHZ circuit na may ibinigay na laki gamit ang breadth-first search sa coupling map, na nagpapakalat ng mga CNOT layer nang parallel para mabawasan ang circuit depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`weighted_coverage`, `active_wires`, `z_trace_backward` — Compute how much of the GHZ circuit's error surface is protected by a given set of spacetime parity checks, using the backward-propagation technique from [[6]](#references).\n"
msgstr "`weighted_coverage`, `active_wires`, `z_trace_backward` — Kinukwenta kung gaano karami sa error surface ng GHZ circuit ang protektado ng isang hanay ng mga spacetime parity check, gamit ang backward-propagation technique mula sa [[6]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`add_measurements` — Appends GHZ-qubit and check-qubit measurements into separate classical registers so they can be postselected independently.\n"
msgstr "`add_measurements` — Nagdaragdag ng mga measurement ng GHZ-qubit at check-qubit sa magkahiwalay na classical register para maaari silang i-postselect nang magkahiwalay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`build_shadow_circuits` — Produces one circuit per random Pauli basis by appending the appropriate single-qubit rotations before measurement.\n"
msgstr "`build_shadow_circuits` — Gumagawa ng isang circuit bawat random Pauli basis sa pamamagitan ng pagdaragdag ng angkop na mga single-qubit rotation bago ang measurement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`parse_hw_results_w_checks` — Unpacks the Sampler output into `(ghz_bits, check_bits, bases)` triples, one per shot.\n"
msgstr "`parse_hw_results_w_checks` — Ina-unpack ang output ng Sampler sa mga triple na `(ghz_bits, check_bits, bases)`, isa bawat shot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`adapt_to_flat_bits`, `estimate_zz_nn_hw` — Map the GHZ-register bits back into the full-device index space and compute the median-of-means $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ estimate.\n"
msgstr "`adapt_to_flat_bits`, `estimate_zz_nn_hw` — Ima-map pabalik ang mga bit ng GHZ-register sa buong index space ng device at kinukwenta ang median-of-means na estimate ng $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Maliit na simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, prepare a 10-qubit GHZ state using statevector simulation and estimate its properties using local Pauli shadows. The GHZ state is a maximally entangled quantum state with three or more qubits serving as a benchmark for multipartite entanglement. It is a common building block for quantum communication and cryptography protocols. Additionally, the GHZ circuit has fully known analytical properties, making it ideal for verification in this tutorial.\n"
msgstr "Una, maghanda ng 10-qubit na GHZ state gamit ang statevector simulation at i-estimate ang mga katangian nito gamit ang mga local Pauli shadow. Ang GHZ state ay isang maximally entangled na quantum state na may tatlo o higit pang qubit na nagsisilbing benchmark para sa multipartite entanglement. Karaniwan itong building block para sa mga quantum communication at cryptography protocol. Bukod dito, ang GHZ circuit ay may ganap na kilalang analytical na mga katangian, kaya mainam ito para sa verification sa tutorial na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang mga classical input sa isang quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare an ideal 10-qubit GHZ state.\n"
msgstr "Maghanda ng ideal na 10-qubit na GHZ state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize para sa pagpapatakbo sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, define a function that collects shadow snapshots by rotating the GHZ state into random Pauli bases. This mirrors what the Sampler primitive does on hardware in the large-scale example.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, mag-define ng function na nangongolekta ng mga shadow snapshot sa pamamagitan ng pag-rotate ng GHZ state sa mga random na Pauli basis. Ginagaya nito ang ginagawa ng Sampler primitive sa hardware sa malakihang halimbawa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Patakbuhin gamit ang mga Qiskit primitive {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this simulation, use the statevector directly.\n"
msgstr "Para sa simulation na ito, gamitin nang direkta ang statevector.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the shadow estimator and the median-of-means (MOM) estimator for the random measurement bases used to collect the shadow snapshots. Use these functions to estimate properties of the GHZ state, including single-qubit magnetization, two-qubit correlators, and the two-qubit RDM, from the collected measurements. Then compare the estimates with the exact values.\n"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang shadow estimator at ang median-of-means (MOM) estimator para sa mga random na measurement basis na ginamit sa pagkolekta ng mga shadow snapshot. Gamitin ang mga function na ito para tantiyahin ang mga katangian ng GHZ state, kasama ang single-qubit magnetization, two-qubit correlator, at two-qubit RDM, mula sa mga nakolektang measurement. Pagkatapos, ihambing ang mga tantiya sa eksaktong mga halaga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the results {#visualize-the-results}"
msgstr "I-visualize ang mga resulta {#visualize-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first plot shows the estimated single-qubit magnetization values for the different qubits. The second plot shows the distribution of estimated two-point correlator values for all qubit pairs. The final plot shows the magnitude of the two-qubit reduced density matrix entries. A fairly large collection of snapshots is used for the given system size, so the results are close to the exact ones.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng unang plot ang tinantiyang mga halaga ng single-qubit magnetization para sa iba't ibang qubit. Ipinapakita ng pangalawang plot ang distribusyon ng tinantiyang mga halaga ng two-point correlator para sa lahat ng pares ng qubit. Ipinapakita ng huling plot ang magnitude ng mga entry ng two-qubit reduced density matrix. Medyo malaking koleksyon ng mga snapshot ang ginamit para sa laki ng sistema, kaya malapit sa eksakto ang mga resulta.\n"

