msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/shadow-tomography/extracted-outputs/5da0364f-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa sa malaking-sukat na hardware {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The preceding simulation confirms that local Pauli shadow tomography recovers the correct observables on a noiseless statevector. Running the same protocol using 100 qubits on real hardware introduces two challenges that do not appear in simulation: gate and readout errors accumulate across the deep GHZ circuit, and finding the optimal qubit layout requires searching the device's coupling graph rather than choosing a layout by hand.\n"
msgstr "Kinukumpirma ng naunang simulation na naibabalik ng local Pauli shadow tomography ang tamang mga observable sa isang noiseless na statevector. Ang pagpapatakbo ng parehong protocol gamit ang 100 qubit sa totoong hardware ay nagdudulot ng dalawang hamon na wala sa simulation: nag-iipon ang mga error ng gate at readout sa buong malalim na GHZ circuit, at ang paghahanap ng pinakamainam na layout ng qubit ay nangangailangan ng paghahanap sa coupling graph ng device sa halip na pumili ng layout nang mano-mano.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To address the first challenge, use low-overhead error detection with spacetime codes [[6]](#references). A small number of ancilla qubits adjacent to the GHZ tree are used as parity checks. Each ancilla is entangled with two of its GHZ neighbors before measurement, so a single bit-flip error on either neighbor flips the ancilla's outcome from `0` to `1`. Snapshots where any check ancilla reads `1` are discarded, leaving a cleaner subset from which to estimate $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Para tugunan ang unang hamon, gumamit ng low-overhead error detection gamit ang mga spacetime code [[6]](#references). Isang maliit na bilang ng mga ancilla qubit na katabi ng GHZ tree ang ginagamit bilang mga parity check. Ang bawat ancilla ay ine-entangle sa dalawa sa mga kapitbahay nitong GHZ bago ang measurement, kaya ang isang bit-flip error sa alinmang kapitbahay ay babaligtarin ang resulta ng ancilla mula `0` patungong `1`. Itinatapon ang mga snapshot kung saan nagbabasa ng `1` ang anumang check ancilla, na nag-iiwan ng mas malinis na subset para tantiyahin ang $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second challenge is handled by searching over candidate GHZ tree layouts and selecting the one that maximizes parity-check coverage, that is, the fraction of circuit wires monitored by at least one check, within an acceptable increase in circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "Ang pangalawang hamon ay tinutugunan sa pamamagitan ng paghahanap sa mga kandidatong layout ng GHZ tree at pagpili sa isa na nagpapalaki ng parity-check coverage, ibig sabihin, ang bahagi ng mga wire ng circuit na binabantayan ng kahit isang check, sa loob ng katanggap-tanggap na pagtaas ng circuit depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1-4 (performed in a single code block) {#steps-1-4-performed-in-a-single-code-block}"
msgstr "Mga Hakbang 1-4 (isinasagawa sa iisang code block) {#steps-1-4-performed-in-a-single-code-block}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same four-step workflow is now applied to a 100-qubit GHZ state on real quantum hardware, adding two hardware-specific features that do not arise in simulation:\n"
msgstr "Ang parehong four-step na workflow ay inilalapat na ngayon sa isang 100-qubit na GHZ state sa totoong quantum hardware, na nagdaragdag ng dalawang feature na partikular sa hardware na hindi lumilitaw sa simulation:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1** characterizes the backend noise (gate errors, readout errors, and T2 times) so that unreliable qubits and edges are excluded from the circuit layout.\n"
msgstr "**Hakbang 1** ay nagpapakilala sa noise ng backend (mga error ng gate, mga error ng readout, at mga oras ng T2) para hindi isama sa layout ng circuit ang mga hindi maaasahang qubit at edge.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 2** searches over possible GHZ tree layouts to find one that maximizes parity-check coverage within an acceptable circuit depth — replacing the trivial chain used in simulation.\n"
msgstr "**Hakbang 2** ay naghahanap sa mga posibleng layout ng GHZ tree para makahanap ng isa na nagpapalaki ng parity-check coverage sa loob ng katanggap-tanggap na circuit depth — pinapalitan ang simpleng chain na ginamit sa simulation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 3** builds the shadow circuits (one per random Pauli basis), transpiles them to hardware-native gates, and submits them to the Sampler primitive with `shots=8` (each circuit produces eight independent bitstrings).\n"
msgstr "**Hakbang 3** ay bumubuo ng mga shadow circuit (isa para sa bawat random na Pauli basis), nagta-transpile sa mga ito sa mga hardware-native na gate, at nagsusumite sa mga ito sa Sampler primitive na may `shots=8` (bawat circuit ay gumagawa ng walong independiyenteng bitstring).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 4** postselects snapshots whose check qubits all read 0 (no detected error), then estimates $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ with and without that postselection to demonstrate the improvement from error detection.\n"
msgstr "**Hakbang 4** ay nagpo-postselect ng mga snapshot kung saan lahat ng check qubit ay nagbabasa ng 0 (walang natukoy na error), pagkatapos ay tinatantiya ang $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ na mayroon at walang postselection na iyon para ipakita ang pagbuti mula sa error detection.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/shadow-tomography/extracted-outputs/502e92dd-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/shadow-tomography/extracted-outputs/502e92dd-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interpret the results {#interpret-the-results}"
msgstr "Bigyang-kahulugan ang mga resulta {#interpret-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two plots show $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ estimated from shadow tomography for each neighboring qubit pair in the 100-qubit GHZ chain, before and after postselecting on the parity checks.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng dalawang plot ang $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ na tinantiya mula sa shadow tomography para sa bawat magkatabing pares ng qubit sa 100-qubit na GHZ chain, bago at pagkatapos mag-postselect sa mga parity check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For an ideal GHZ state, all nearest-neighbor correlators equal $1$. On hardware, noise depresses the raw estimates and introduces qubit-to-qubit scatter. After error detection, snapshots in which at least one detectable error occurred are removed, and the remaining estimates are pulled closer to $1$ with reduced variance, which is consistent with a cleaner effective state.\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang ideal na GHZ state, lahat ng nearest-neighbor correlator ay katumbas ng $1$. Sa hardware, ibinababa ng noise ang mga raw na tantiya at nagdudulot ng scatter mula qubit patungong qubit. Pagkatapos ng error detection, inaalis ang mga snapshot kung saan nagkaroon ng kahit isang natutukoy na error, at ang natitirang mga tantiya ay mas lumalapit sa $1$ na may mas maliit na variance, na naaayon sa mas malinis na epektibong state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The improvement after error detection is consistent with the checks detecting real errors.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagbuti pagkatapos ng error detection ay naaayon sa mga check na nakakakita ng totoong mga error.\n"

